{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"0e33ba0e43cf7d50","type":"text","text":"# **26 November 2026 | 2 VWO**\n### Alice in Wonderland | Lesson 2 of 3","x":-360,"y":-335,"width":650,"height":80,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"9c76dfc69779aa67","type":"text","text":"## **Today | 30 minutes**\n**0–3 min**  Quick review of yesterday\n**3–6 min**  Predict (Q1)\n**6–12 min**  Read and skim (Q2)\n**12–18 min**  TASK + evidence (Q3–5)\n**18–22 min**  False friends (Q6)\n**22–27 min**  Present perfect + advice (Q7–8)\n**27–30 min**  Exit ticket (Q9)","x":-360,"y":-225,"width":650,"height":252,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"f3fa5a630ebd8478","type":"text","text":"# **Homework**\nWrite a **3-line dialogue** between Alice and a friend.\n\nUse **one present perfect form** and **two modals**.","x":-360,"y":55,"width":650,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"fd2d0809e8e04270","type":"text","text":"## **Class routine**\n1. Follow the text without changing its words.\n2. Work **individually first**, then with your assigned partner.\n3. Use **voice level 0** or **1** as instructed.\n4. When time is up, finish your sentence and listen.","x":-360,"y":281,"width":650,"height":186,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"44a5f97dd3995de7","type":"text","text":"## **Big question**\nWho are you? Why does Alice struggle to answer?","x":450,"y":-335,"width":600,"height":112,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"a5436460730e2406","type":"text","text":"## **Learning goals**\n**I can:** explain Alice’s problem; copy **one** clue; infer tone from words; recognise false friends; use the present perfect and supportive modals.","x":450,"y":-195,"width":600,"height":154,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"41c61f19364c69e2","type":"text","text":"**0–3 | Retrieval, silence**\nWhat happened to Alice in Lesson 1? Write **one** idea and **one** advice sentence with *should*.\n\n**3–6 | Prediction**\nDo **Q1**: write **one possible reason** someone might feel confused about who they are.","x":450,"y":-10,"width":600,"height":195,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"db52f124037cd113","type":"text","text":"## **TASK before every answer**\n**T** Task: circle the instruction word.\n**A** Answer: letter, phrase or full sentence?\n**S** Special conditions: *exactly*, *copy*, *English*, *two*.\n**K** Keep checking: did you follow **all** instructions?\n\n**Reading focus:** skim dialogue; scan for a **direct clue**; interpret tone.\n**Team roles:** Question Decoder / Evidence Finder.\n**Voice level:** 0 reading, 1 pair work.","x":450,"y":218,"width":600,"height":230,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"9b77fca3437450ae","type":"text","text":"## **Original novel | Chapter V: Advice from a Caterpillar**\n*Lewis Carroll, Alice’s Adventures in Wonderland (1865)*\n\n> The Caterpillar and Alice looked at each other for some time in silence: at last the Caterpillar took the hookah out of its mouth, and addressed her in a languid, sleepy voice.\n\n> ‘Who are you?’ said the Caterpillar.\n\n> This was not an encouraging opening for a conversation. Alice replied, rather shyly, ‘I--I hardly know, sir, just at present-- at least I know who I was when I got up this morning, but I think I must have been changed several times since then.’\n\n> ‘What do you mean by that?’ said the Caterpillar sternly. ‘Explain yourself!’\n\n> ‘I can't explain myself, I'm afraid, sir’ said Alice, ‘because I'm not myself, you see.’\n\n> ‘I don't see,’ said the Caterpillar.\n\n> ‘I'm afraid I can't put it more clearly,’ Alice replied very politely, ‘for I can't understand it myself to begin with; and being so many different sizes in a day is very confusing.’","x":1140,"y":-335,"width":830,"height":705},
		{"id":"402bcb23fd2a4e4e","type":"text","text":"## **Context and vocabulary support**\nAlice has changed size several times and meets a Caterpillar who asks a difficult question.\n\n**Mini-glossary outside the original:**\n*Caterpillar* = rups\n*languid* = loom\n*sternly* = streng\n\nThe historical story mentions a hookah; the task is about language.","x":1140,"y":400,"width":830,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"c561b76ddf92a784","type":"text","text":"**6–12 | Read the original conversation**\nListen to the voices: who sounds **shy**? Who sounds **stern**?\n\n**Q2:** skim the passage. Choose **A, B or C** and write only the letter.","x":2050,"y":-335,"width":630,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"f76f50a883a72729","type":"text","text":"**12–18 | TASK + evidence in pairs**\n**Q3:** copy **ONE short phrase** showing that Alice feels unsure.\n**Q4:** explain whether *copy* allows a Dutch translation. **Yes/no + 5–10 English words.**\n**Q5:** match *sternly*, *confusing*, *at present* with their meanings.","x":2050,"y":-107,"width":630,"height":230,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"574ad03e2c5f638c","type":"text","text":"**18–22 | False-friend detective**\n**Q6:** choose what **eventually** and **actual** mean in the *new* examples.\n\nThese are teacher-written sentences, not lines from Carroll.","x":2050,"y":151,"width":630,"height":174,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"09bfc34f7f5de3c1","type":"text","text":"**22–27 | Individual language lab**\n**Q7:** complete TWO sentences with **has + past participle** (*change*, *ask*).\n**Q8:** write one kind sentence with **should / could**, plus one with **doesn’t have to**.\n\nOriginal text: **must have been changed** is not the simple pattern from Grammar 3.","x":2050,"y":354,"width":630,"height":218,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"0bdc494487051592","type":"text","text":"**27–30 | Exit ticket: Q9**\nName Alice’s feeling in **ONE word** and give **ONE exact clue** from the text.","x":2050,"y":601,"width":630,"height":164,"color":"1"}
	],
